                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Medieval playground is a sandbox game, developed in Unity engine, or at least it aims to be. And by that I mean that the game is currently in Early Access and what looks like a very early alpha build.\nIt has a very ambitious TODO list and if even 80% of what is there, is implemented it will be a very good game. Right now it looks kind of like an early alpha of Ark. Being not much more than a terrain editor.\n\nGameplay:\nLike I said in the premise. This is currently not in a state that you may actually call it a game. It's more like a terrain editor currently. It is very early in its development cycle, and as such, reviewing it at this point is probably not the best thing to do.\n\n\nGraphics:\nGraphics-wise the engine has potential and the game doesn't look bad. But on a GTX 970 that I played it on, it looks rather unoptimized at this point and there were a few graphics glitches like shimmering textures. All these are to be expected though as it is a very early build.\n\nMusic/Sound Design:\nMusic sounds absolutely great. And there's also an on/off toggle. Sound effects also sound good.\n\nPros:\n-Very ambitious project.\n\nNeutral:\n-Not much is implemented yet so you can't really form a proper opinion.\n\nCons:\n-There's not much of a game yet.\n\nConclusion:\nThis is one of those cases where the binary options don't work. The project looks very ambitious and if it indeed implements everything planned it could become a great game. At this point I can not recommend it, unless someone wants to be actively involved in its development and support the project.\n\nScore:\nGameplay:          3/10\nGraphics:\t\t    8/10\nMusic/Sound:\t    9/10\nConcept/Story:    6/10\n\n\nMore game reviews @ https://cassus.org",
